        <Section title="4. Critical quality points and agreed controls"><ol className="space-y-2 list-decimal pl-5">{meeting.critical.map(point => <li key={point}>{point}</li>)}</ol><p><strong>First-output and process checks:</strong> Production retains the approved first piece at the line. Inline QC checks the agreed critical operations and records style, line, operation, defect, quantity and time. Nonconforming work is separated and returns through repair and reinspection.</p><p><strong>Sampling and acceptance:</strong> The effective technical reference and order control plan define tolerances, test methods, inspection frequency and defect classes. Final inspection uses the agreed buyer sampling plan; a pilot pass is not final shipment release.</p></Section>
